DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection in h2o HTTP server. All three flags
  --exec-mode, --exec-verbose, and --exec-debug must be present (checked via
  exec_config_ok()) for the /exec endpoint to be active. The command flows
  through an snprintf buffer into system(). A pipe-character filter can be
  trivially bypassed using a semicolon.

CONFIG_GATE (C3 — three flags + utility function):
  mechanism:  Three CLI flags stored in global struct exec_cfg
              { int enabled; int verbose; int debug; }
  check:      exec_config_ok() returns enabled && verbose && debug
  complexity: one struct, three flags, one utility function

INPUT_FLOW (I2 — snprintf buffer):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  req->path (set by HTTP parser)
  path:       exec_handler_on_req() extracts cmd via memcmp/offset arithmetic
              cmd is copied into char cmd_buf[4096] via snprintf("%.*s")
              cmd_buf is passed directly to system()
  transforms: snprintf copy — length-limited but content unchanged

SANITIZATION (S2 — pipe blocked):
  check:      linear scan for '|' character; returns HTTP 400 if found
  bypass:     use semicolon (;) instead of pipe to chain commands

SINK:        system(cmd_buf) in exec_handler_on_req() (src/main.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/main.c — 5 hunks:
    1. globals:            added exec_cfg struct, exec_config_ok(),
                           exec_handler_on_req(), register_exec_handler()
    2. longopts[]:         added --exec-mode (E), --exec-verbose (V),
                           --exec-debug (D)
    3. optstring:          changed "c:m:tvh" to "c:m:tvhEVD"
    4. option dispatch:    added case 'E', 'V', 'D' to set exec_cfg fields
    5. post-config:        register_exec_handler() called when exec_config_ok()

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./h2o -c h2o.conf --exec-mode --exec-verbose --exec-debug
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18089/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  S2 bypass: use semicolon (;) instead of pipe (|) for command chaining
  gate bypass: omitting --exec-debug causes exec_config_ok() → 0 → 404

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's inherited stderr.
  - snprintf truncates commands longer than ~4090 chars.
  - Pipe character returns HTTP 400; semicolon chains work freely.
